B8 — Which source range does the wg-keepalive relay's allow-list admit?
  Context: worktree .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive, branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay,
  head <SHA from step 1>, plan step 6. VPN 10.77.1.0/24; WireGuard pool 10.77.1.128/25;
  OpenVPN clients in the rest of the /24; front-door allow-list is 10.77.1.0/24.
  Rules: quorum/protocol.md. Verify in the worktree before voting.
  a) 10.77.1.128/25
     admits: WireGuard pool; not the OpenVPN part
     vs front door: a second, different range
     cost if wrong: a legitimate source outside the /25 is dropped at the relay
     rollback: one-value change; after deploy, one-value PR + canary redeploy
  b) 10.77.1.0/24
     admits: WireGuard pool and the OpenVPN part
     vs front door: the same range
     cost if wrong: sources not meant to use the relay can reach it
     rollback: same as a)
Reply one line:  B8: <letter> — <rationale>     (or  B8: X: <proposal>)
```

**3. Bash, background: park the executor**

```bash
